# Git, terminal, and lint

## Git commands — only when

- The user explicitly asks to commit, create a PR, or inspect git history
- Do not run `git status`, `git diff`, or `git log` on every turn

## Shell commands

- Do not run a terminal command when `grep` or `read` answers the question
- Avoid long-running commands whose output fills context (full builds, install logs)

## Linting

- Run linter diagnostics only on files you edited, not the whole workspace
- This project has no automated test suite — do not run test commands unless tests are added and the user asks
